    </header>

    <p class="lede">"How long until my solar pays for itself?" is the question that determines whether residential solar is a financial decision or an environmental one. In 2026, the answer ranges from six years to never depending on your state — and the variables are not the ones most homeowners think they are. This guide walks through the actual math, the net-metering policy that drives most of the variance, and why the federal credit expiration changes the calculation more than panel costs.</p>
